    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2054097207574364515",
      "url": "https://x.com/ObaiBiOlorun/status/2054097207574364515",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ObaiBiOlorun/status/2054097207574364515",
      "text": "the part most new freelancers need to hear is buried in the middle\n\nstop pitching established clients and go find clients who just joined the platform\n\nnew client, new freelancer… the playing field is actually level there\n\nthe location bias point is also real and underrated… India and Philippines didn’t build those reputations by accident, they built niche dominance over years\n\nNigeria is getting there but we’re still in the trust-building phase which means you have to outwork the reputation gap\n\nand the $1000 on Connects point reframes everything\n\nfreelancing isn’t a skill game alone, it’s a client acquisition game\n\nthe ones winning understand that one solid long term client pays back every dollar spent finding them…may God help us all",
